accepted in few cultures (Samoa?).  I think all such experiments in
this country have failed.

In reference to the "Subject:", in college (before I was exposed to
Ayn Rand) I found the culture/society of "Brave New World," with its
free and easy sex, freedom from responsibility, and "everybody's
happy" (except the Indian misfit) to be very attractive. Why were they
telling me this was a DYStopia?  Also I found (and still find) the
society of Frederic Pohl's "Age of the Pussyfoot," very appealing;
although I'm not sure he meant it to be. I recommend it as one of the
very few -optimistic- (though not problem-free) cryonics stories.

"Unofficlal" polygamy, i.e.  extra-marital liasons can be fun.  Before
my first marriage I attended several "Sexual Freedom League" parties
where husbands brought their wives to "trade" for an evening.  During
my first marriage I took a "batchelor holiday" in Thailand.  But such
activities seem to be very risky to the stability of the primary
relationship.  (And these days are a medical risk as well). I wouldn't
